export const CORE_LESSONS = "# Lessons\n\nEverything this framework learned the hard way, one line each. Read the whole file — that is the\npoint of it being this short. The long version of any line lives in the module header it names.\n\nFormat: `DOMAIN  what is true → what to do instead`. A line earns its place by having cost a\nsession; if it is merely good advice, it belongs in a module header, not here.\n\n## Properties the engine owns\n\nAn engine system rewrites these every frame. A write reverts before it is drawn, and — the\nexpensive part — anything you measure through one comes back as a plausible wrong number.\n`Util.Holds.check(instance, property, value)` settles it in two frames.\n\n```\nPROPERTY  Motor6D.Transform is rewritten by the Animator on every joint, animated or not\n          → drive a custom joint through C0\nPROPERTY  AnimationConstraint.Transform likewise; a 60° drive measured 1.7°\n          → publish an animation asset\nPROPERTY  LocalTransparencyModifier is reset on a part as it joins a character; it holds on one\n          that has been there a while, which is why it tests as working\n          → write Transparency\nINPUT     Humanoid.MoveDirection is read-only and the control script calls Move every frame\n          → drive the character from the server, sample on the client\nPROPERTY  A Highlight with Adornee = nil outlines its Parent; parented to Workspace, \"clear\n          the outline\" outlines the whole world\n          → toggle Enabled; never clear Adornee to hide it\n```\n\n## Rigs and animation\n\n```\nRIG       R15 joins with AnimationConstraint, not Motor6D; server-side arm posing does nothing\n          → publish a KeyframeSequence, see docs in the game's animation-pipeline\nRIG       KeyframeSequence.Priority is lost on RegisterKeyframeSequence\n          → set track.Priority after LoadAnimation\nUPLOAD    Open Cloud rejects .rbxm animations sent as application/octet-stream\n          → model/x-rbxm\n```\n\n## State and data\n\n```\nSTATE     A listener added before its key binds is retained and fires on bind\n          → never poll Data.loaded before observing; a deadline only throws away the late case\nSTATE     A key written and never read leaves no trace at runtime: set, replicated, saved, unread\n          → run the `unread` command after adding a saved key\nDATA      ProfileStore waits six times five seconds for a session lock before taking it\n          → Studio takes it at once; 30s of \"slow DataStore\" is this\nDATA      A character spawns before its profile binds\n          → draw saved stock by following the value, never by reading it once\n```\n\n## Studio and the edit session\n\n```\nSTUDIO    require is cached per ModuleScript and Rojo rewrites Source in place; restarting\n          Studio does not clear it, and cloning the test still runs the cached module the\n          test requires, so a passing or failing run can be about code you deleted\n          → clone the module under test too and repoint the test's require at the clone;\n            check .Source for a string you just wrote before believing any result\nLUAU      A table key past ~2^24 leaves the array part for the hash part; ids built as\n          slot + generation * stride cross that line the moment anything recycles, so a\n          benchmark on a fresh world can be 1.5x faster than the same code in production\n          → key hot tables by the dense small int, and benchmark a recycled world\nSTUDIO    Renaming a Rojo mount leaves the old instances behind, running a second copy\n          → delete them by hand after any mount rename\nSTUDIO    A project file change needs `rojo serve` restarted and the plugin reconnected\nSTUDIO    The playtest an agent drives is the one the user is playing in; a test that\n          anchors or moves their character and does not undo it reads to them as a broken game\n          → release the root (Anchored = false) before every eval returns, error path included\n```\n\n## Replication and effects\n\n```\nNET       Cosmetics are not worth a remote each; a frame's worth batches into one call per\n          nearby player\n          → Server/Core/NearbyVfx, received by shared/Effects\nNET       Anything both sides can derive from the same inputs should not be sent\n          → send the owner and the slot, derive the seed\nCLIENT    A client may move an anchored part the server owns and it stays moved, because the\n          server never corrects a part it is not moving\n          → always write rest * offset from a stored rest, never step from the current value\n```\n\n## Measuring\n\n```\nMEASURE   A settling value sampled too early is indistinguishable from permanent drift\n          → compare against the server's own value, and sample twice seconds apart\nMEASURE   A harness that holds a movement key for seconds measures the harness, not the feature\nMEASURE   Identical numbers from two different inputs mean the input never landed\n```\n\n## Shape of the framework\n\n```\nSHAPE     Server modules are instances: `.new(options)` with an exported Options type, and a\n          clock or Random injected where behaviour depends on them. That is what the specs need.\nSHAPE     Shared modules are singletons, as Knit's Services are. Correct for one-per-server\n          things; it is why two differently configured instances are not possible.\nSHAPE     Systems.start is the scheduler. `first` is an ordering list you maintain by hand —\n          there is no Init/Start split, so a system that needs another at boot must say so.\nSHAPE     A mechanism moves here once a second game wants it, not before.\n```\n";
